// spec: an array's bound that is no constant expression (a division by zero in the function it calls) is an error at the declaration, as in C++, never an array of no elements
// error: array_bound_that_is_no_constant_is_error.kpp:6: error:
// factorio: found by the templates thread: convertType made `int sized[broken(3)]` an array of 0 elements when the bound did not evaluate (and so did a bound calling a function declared before its definition)
// pending: an array bound that does not evaluate is silently 0
constexpr int broken(int v) { return v / 0; }
int sized[broken(3)];
int main()
{
  println("{}", int(sizeof(sized) / sizeof(int)));
  return 0;
}
